sular. et Bruttiorum antiquæ tabulæ, cum animadversionib","Amico, 1741","Castelli, 1769","Castelli, 1784, Siciliae et objacentium insularum veterum inscriptionum nova collectio prolegomenis et notis illustrata, et iterum cum emendationibus, & auctariis evulgata","Ferrara, 1829, Storia di Catania sino alla fine del secolo XVIII","Kaibel, 1890, IG","Korhonen, 2004, IMusCatania","Boeckh, Franz, 1853, CIG","Libertini, 1930, Il Museo Biscari",[273,274,275,276,277,278,279,280,281],"ZP8DE8KS","F5INCW3T","SPTB56H3","7PSFHSUH","82T4IWDN","Q2SBPG9F","2EUC82DH","TQMVHEVL","SKUU2R8X",[283,284,285,24,29,33,286,287,288,289,287,290,291,124],"isic001325","epitaph for sosia elate",{"_":5},"catina","catania","sicilia","sicily","museo civico di catania","ancient greek",[],{"title":294,"body":295,"divs":296,"editions":317,"images":327,"handnote":328},"ISic001325. Epitaph for Sosia Elate","\u003Cdiv id=\"editions\">\u003Cdiv class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Marta Fogagnolo\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv id=\"edition-interpretive\" lang=\"grc\">  \u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\" lang=\"grc\">\u003Cspan class=\"ab\" id=\"div-interpretive\">  \u003Ca id=\"al1-interpretive\">\u003C!--0-->\u003C/a>\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">1\u003C/span>\u003Cspan data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"attested\" data-text=\"Σοσίᾳ  Ἐλάτῃ\">\u003Cspan data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Σοσίᾳ\">Σοσίᾳ\u003C/span>  \u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\">(vac.2)\u003C/span>  \u003Cspan data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Ἐλάτῃ\">Ἐλάτῃ\u003C/span>\u003C/span>  \u003Cbr id=\"al2-interpretive\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">2\u003C/span>\u003Cspan data-text=\"γλυκυτάτῃ\">γλυκυτάτῃ\u003C/span>  \u003Cbr id=\"al3-interpretive\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">3\u003C/span>\u003Cspan data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"attested\" data-text=\"Ἀφροδείσιος\">\u003Cspan data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Ἀφροδείσιος\">Ἀφροδείσιος\u003C/span>\u003C/span>  \u003Cbr id=\"al4-interpretive\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">4\u003C/span>\u003Cspan data-text=\"σύμβιος\">σύμβιος\u003C/span>  \u003C/span>\u003C/div>  \u003Cp class=\"miniapp\">\u003C/p>\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Marta Fogagnolo\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv id=\"edition-diplomatic\" lang=\"grc\">\u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\" lang=\"grc\">\u003Cspan class=\"ab\" id=\"div-diplomatic\">\u003Ca id=\"al1-diplomatic\">\u003C!--0-->\u003C/a>\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">1\u003C/span>\u003Cspan data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"attested\" data-text=\"Σοσίᾳ  Ἐλάτῃ\">\u003Cspan data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Σοσίᾳ\">ΣΟΣΙΑ\u003C/span> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; \u003Cspan data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Ἐλάτῃ\">ΕΛΑΤΗ\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003Cbr id=\"al2-diplomatic\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">2\u003C/span>\u003Cspan data-text=\"γλυκυτάτῃ\">ΓΛΥΚΥΤΑΤΗ\u003C/span>\u003Cbr id=\"al3-diplomatic\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">3\u003C/span>\u003Cspan data-type=\"persname\" data-name-type=\"attested\" data-text=\"Ἀφροδείσιος\">\u003Cspan data-type=\"name\" data-name-type=\"\" data-text=\"Ἀφροδείσιος\">ΑΦΡΟΔΕΙΣΙΟΣ\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003Cbr id=\"al4-diplomatic\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">4\u003C/span>\u003Cspan data-text=\"σύμβιος\">ΣΥΜΒΙΟΣ\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/div>\u003Cp class=\"miniapp\">\u003C/p>\u003C/div>\u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"facsimile-images\">\u003Ch2>Facsimile Images\u003C/h2>\u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"apparatus\">\u003Ch4>Apparatus criticus\u003C/h4>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003Cspan>\u003Cspan>Text based on photographs\u003C/span>\u003C/span>; \u003C/li>\u003Cli>\u003Cspan class=\"1-2\">1-2: \u003Cspan>Korhonen observes that the name of the deceased could be in the nominative form, but the presence of the attribute suggests that it is dative.\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/li>\u003C/ul>\u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"translation\">\u003Ch2>English translation\u003C/h2>\u003Cp class=\"translation-author\">\u003Ca href=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5187-5163\">Marta Fogagnolo\u003C/a>\u003C/p>  \u003Cp>To the sweetest Sosia Elate, Aphrodeisios, her husband.\u003C/p>  \u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"translation\">\u003Ch2>Italian translation\u003C/h2>\u003Cp class=\"translation-author\">\u003Ca href=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5187-5163\">Marta Fogagnolo\u003C/a>\u003C/p>  \u003Cp>Alla dolcissima Sosia Elate, Aphrodisios, il marito.\u003C/p>  \u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"commentary\">\u003Ch2>commentary\u003C/h2>  \u003Cp>The epitaph presents a less common structure, with the name of the deceased probably in dative and the name of the dedicant in nominative followed by an attribute that qualifies his relationship with the deceased (see Korhonen 2004: 87). To be excluded is the interpretation of the epitaph as two nominatives, the first of the name of the deceased, the latter of the name of the dedicant because of the attribute \u003Cspan class=\"lang\" lang=\"grc\">γλυκυτάτη\u003C/span>. The indication of the age of the deceased and the dedication verb is omitted. The gentilicium Sosia testifies that the deceased belonged the gens Sosia; her cognomen \u003Cspan class=\"lang\" lang=\"grc\">Ἐλάτη\u003C/span> is also attested in an inscription of imperial age from Dikaiarchia-Puteoli (CIL 10.2209). The name of the husband, \u003Cspan class=\"lang\" lang=\"grc\">Ἀφροδείσιος\u003C/span>, is well attested in several inscriptions of South Italy (LGPN 3A: 86).\u003C/p>  \u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"bibliography\">\u003Ch2>bibliography\u003C/h2>  \u003Cul>\u003Cli> Gualtherus 1624 [1625] 45 \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001931\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001931\u003C/a>\u003C/li>\u003Cli> Amico 1741 246 no.1 \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002186\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002186\u003C/a>\u003C/li>\u003Cli> Castelli 1769 142 no.43 \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002084\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002084\u003C/a>\u003C/li>\u003Cli> Castelli 1784 149 no.50 \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002083\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002083\u003C/a>\u003C/li>\u003Cli> Ferrara 1829 345 no.1 \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002005\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002005\u003C/a>\u003C/li>\u003Cli> Franz 1853 5706 \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001250\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001250\u003C/a>\u003C/li>\u003Cli> Kaibel 1890 \u003Ca href=\"https://clio.columbia.edu/catalog/6873760\" target=\"_blank\">504\u003C/a>  \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001072\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001072\u003C/a>\u003C/li>\u003Cli> Libertini 1930 73 no.152 ph \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001871\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001871\u003C/a>\u003C/li>\u003Cli> Korhonen 2004 129 \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10000028\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10000028\u003C/a>\u003C/li>\u003C/ul>  \u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003C/li>\u003C/ul>  \u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"handnote\">\u003Cp>Regular letters: lunate Ε, Σ, cursive Μ. Φ with an extended upright and Υ at l. 4 with extended slanted bars.\u003C/p> Lines 1-4  17-25  Interlineation line 1 to 2  not recorded  \u003C/div>\u003Cdiv id=\"license\"> Licensed under a Creative Commons-Attribution 4.0 licence. \u003C/div>",[297,300,303,306,308,311,314],{"id":298,"html":299},"editions","\u003Cdiv class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Marta Fogagnolo\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv id=\"edition-interpretive\" lang=\"grc\">  \u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\" lang=\"grc\">\u003Cspan class=\"ab\" id=\"div-interpretive\">  \u003Ca id=\"al1-interpretive\">\u003C!--0-->\u003C/a>\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\"